# React & JSX Conventions

## Patterns in This Codebase

- **Single-file app**: Main logic lives in `src/App.jsx`. “Conceptual” modules are marked with comments like `// CONCEPTUAL FILE: path/to/thing`; they are inline helpers/components, not real files. When adding new behavior, add it in the same file and keep the comment convention, unless the project has decided to extract real modules.
- **Functional components only**: No class components.
- **State**: `useState` for local UI state; `useEffect` for syncing to localStorage and for loading Marked/KaTeX from CDN.
- **Styling**: Tailwind utility classes. Use `dark:` for dark mode. Prefer existing patterns (e.g. `text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400`, `bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800`).
- **Icons**: Lucide React (e.g. `Github`, `Save`, `FileText`). Import from `lucide-react`.
- **Toasts**: Inline `Toast` component; show by setting toast state (message + type `'error'` or success). No external toast library.

## Do

- Use existing localStorage keys (`markhub_draft`, `gh_token`, `markhub_hidden_repos`, `markhub_local_workspace`, `theme`) when adding persistence.
- Keep accessibility in mind (e.g. `title` on icon buttons, semantic HTML).
- Use `className` for Tailwind; avoid inline styles unless necessary.

## Avoid

- Introducing new global state libraries unless agreed; state is local + localStorage.
- Adding Marked/KaTeX as npm deps without updating the CDN-loading logic in `App.jsx` (or replacing it).
- Breaking the existing view modes (Editor Only, Split, Preview Only) or keyboard shortcuts documented in README.
